# Example environment for local dev/test builds. Copy to `.env.local` (which is
# gitignored) and fill in real values — never commit a real token.
#
# Vite inlines any VITE_-prefixed variable into the built bundle at build time.

# DEVELOPMENT FALLBACK ONLY — not how the companion joins sync.
#
# The relay (sync.minutist.ai) is admission-gated, and what the app presents at
# the gate is the per-device account credential obtained by signing in: the
# RFC 8628 device-code flow in src/account/signin.ts stores that credential, and
# src/sync/capacitor.ts passes it to the engine's start(). That is the mechanism,
# it is implemented, and it is what a shipped build uses.
#
# This variable only covers dev builds with no signed-in account: when no stored
# credential exists, the app falls back to this static token. Vite inlines it
# into the bundle at build time, so it is not secret and must not be used for
# anything but local development against the gated relay. Obtain a current dev
# token from the relay deployment (minutist-relay: deploy/iroh-relay.env).
#
# Prefer signing in. Reach for this only when a build cannot complete sign-in.
VITE_RELAY_AUTH_TOKEN=
